        <detaileddescription>
<para>A buffer is considered overdue when its oldest data point has been held for longer than <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_adaptive_flush_controller_config_1a5b059bf99a6269e44b7ea00cf0e56598" kindref="member">flush_interval</ref> * <ref refid="structthemis_1_1_adaptive_flush_controller_config_1a8a7ac963f066c911343795a08a004744" kindref="member">overdue_flush_multiplier</ref></computeroutput>. An overdue event emits a WARN log and increments the stats counter. Default: 2 (= 2× the flush interval). </para>
        </detaileddescription>
